-- title:
--   Explicit construction, dimension, and classification
-- statement:
--   Let $R$ be a finite reduced irreducible crystallographic root system of positive rank, with a fixed positive system and simple roots $\alpha_i$, Weyl group $W$, and full weight lattice $P$. Fix $q\in\mathbb C^\times$ which is not a root of unity. Write $\widetilde H$ for its affine Hecke algebra with $T_i^2=(q-q^{-1})T_i+1$ and the Bernstein relation with denominator $1-X^{-\alpha_i}$ interpreted as a Laurent-polynomial divided difference. Let $T=\operatorname{Hom}(P,\mathbb C^\times)$, with $(wt)(X^\lambda)=t(X^{w^{-1}\lambda})$. All modules below are finite dimensional complex left modules. Irreducible modules are nonzero.
--
--   For $t\in T$, put $Z(t)=\{\alpha>0:t(X^\alpha)=1\}$ and $P_q(t)=\{\alpha>0:t(X^\alpha)=q^{\pm2}\}$. For $J\subseteq P_q(t)$ let
--   $$F(t,J)=\{w\in W:R(w)\cap Z(t)=\varnothing,\ R(w)\cap P_q(t)=J\},$$
--   where $R(w)=\{\alpha>0:w\alpha<0\}$. A placed skew shape has $F(t,J)\ne\varnothing$ and every $wt$, $w\in F(t,J)$, is simple-root regular and calibratable in every rank-two subsystem generated by simple roots, in the sense of §3.
--
--   Here rank-two calibratability means either every root of the generated subsystem evaluates differently from $1$, or the subsystem has type $C_2$ or $G_2$ and some element of its rank-two Weyl group moves the character to values $q^2$ on the long simple root and $1$ on the short simple root, with both original simple-root evaluations different from $1$.
--
--   For each placed skew shape, the free space on $\{v_w:w\in F(t,J)\}$ has the explicit generator action
--   $$X^\lambda v_w=(wt)(X^\lambda)v_w,\qquad T_i v_w=d_i(wt)v_w+(q^{-1}+d_i(wt))v_{s_iw},\qquad d_i(b)=\frac{q-q^{-1}}{1-b(X^{-\alpha_i})},$$
--   with $v_{s_iw}=0$ if $s_iw\notin F(t,J)$. This action satisfies all defining relations, is irreducible and calibrated, and has dimension $|F(t,J)|$. For a fixed $t$, two such modules are isomorphic exactly when their labels $J$ agree. Every irreducible calibrated module has a central character. Every such module with central character $Wt$ is isomorphic to exactly one such module with base character $t$.
--
--   These statements give the explicit construction and the dimension and isomorphism classification. Simple-root regularity includes the proof-supported rank-one repair; representatives from different base characters are not claimed to give distinct isomorphism classes.
-- source:
--   Calibrated representations of affine Hecke algebras, arXiv:math/0401323v2, PDF p. 1, Abstract; Theorems 3.1 and 4.5

import Definitions.Def_QAlgorithms_Papers_Independent_Intake100_P26

noncomputable section

namespace QAlgorithms.Papers.Independent.Intake100.P26

open scoped BigOperators

variable {D : Datum} {V U : Type*}

variable [AddCommGroup V] [Module ℂ V] [AddCommGroup U] [Module ℂ U]

/-- Abstract, PDF p.1, pinned to Theorems 3.1 and 4.5, PDF pp.12,18:
explicit generators, dimensions, nonisomorphism for fixed t, and exhaustive
classification. The explicit actions live in `tableauGenerators`; no arbitrary
operators satisfying the intended conclusion are substituted for them.
The rank-one and canonical-representative repairs are recorded above. -/
theorem mainResults (D : Datum) (q : ℂ) (hq : GoodParameter q) :
    (∀ (t : Torus D) (J : Set (Fin D.rootCount)), PlacedSkewShape D q t J →
      Relations q (tableauGenerators D q t J) ∧ HeckeIrreducible (tableauGenerators D q t J) ∧
      Calibrated (tableauGenerators D q t J) ∧
      Module.finrank ℂ (TableauSpace D q t J) =
        Nat.card {w : Weyl D // w ∈ tableaux D q t J}) ∧
    (∀ (t : Torus D) (J K : Set (Fin D.rootCount)),
      PlacedSkewShape D q t J → PlacedSkewShape D q t K →
      (HeckeEquivalent (tableauGenerators D q t J) (tableauGenerators D q t K) ↔ J = K)) ∧
    (∀ (V : Type) [AddCommGroup V] [Module ℂ V] [FiniteDimensional ℂ V]
      (A : HeckeGenerators D V), Relations q A → HeckeIrreducible A → Calibrated A →
      (∃ t : Torus D, CentralCharacter A t) ∧
      ∀ t : Torus D, CentralCharacter A t →
      ∃! J : Set (Fin D.rootCount),
        PlacedSkewShape D q t J ∧ HeckeEquivalent A (tableauGenerators D q t J)) := by sorry

end QAlgorithms.Papers.Independent.Intake100.P26

end
